@startuml
title Future application design and delivery dependency boundaries
package "agrosphere-architecture" {
 rectangle "Approved cross-service design" as Arch
}
package "agrosphere-contracts" {
 rectangle "Versioned API / event contracts" as Contracts
}
package "Discovered service repository A" {
 rectangle "Service design and task A" as ServiceA
}
package "Discovered service repository B" {
 rectangle "Service design and task B" as ServiceB
}
package "agrosphere-orchestrator" {
 rectangle "Run manifest / task DAG / artifact hashes" as Run
 rectangle "AEO-5 unit dependency state" as Units
}
Arch --> Contracts : approved impact only
Arch --> ServiceA : design requirement references
Arch --> ServiceB : design requirement references
Contracts --> ServiceA : pinned compatible version
Contracts --> ServiceB : pinned compatible version
Run --> ServiceA : exact isolated execution authority
Run --> ServiceB : only when prerequisites available
ServiceA --> Units : verified commits and QA
ServiceB --> Units : verified commits and QA
note bottom of Units
A PR existing does not make dependency content available.
No sibling source dependency or cross-service SQL.
end note
@enduml
